GCC 14.2.0 for Belka
====================

The release archive and GCC's matching GMP 6.2.1, MPFR 4.1.0 and MPC 1.2.1
prerequisites are pinned by SHA-256 in tools/toolchain/sources. Archives
are cached under build/distfiles; sources are unpacked under
build/toolchain-src. tools/toolchain/prepare.sh verifies the archives and
applies the patches here. It does not execute download_prerequisites.

Upstream sources keep their GPL and LGPL notices and runtime exceptions.
The Belka target header is MIT-licensed. Patches to upstream files retain
those files' licences. The host cross compiler and native compiler are
built separately; both target x86_64-unknown-belka and use illumos ld.
Only the amd64 LP64 ABI is enabled. Multilib, LTO, NLS and optional target
runtimes are disabled for the initial bootstrap.

The native source kit is prepared in build/gcc-bootstrap-src, independently
of the host cross-build sources. libgcc builds Belka's MIT-licensed array
boundary objects from copies of usr/lib/crt, using t-belka. The assembler
probe uses POSIX tail syntax. See doc/native-development.md for the offline
source kit and staged native bootstrap procedure.
